# SYNOPSIS

```text
echo start glmark2 >/svc/launcher/ctl
glmark2-es2-vectraos [--off-screen] [--size WxH] [-b BENCHMARK]...
                     [--run-forever] [-l] [-d]
```

# DESCRIPTION

glmark2-es2-vectraos is glmark2 2023.01, the GLES 2.0 benchmark, as a program of tier 1 in C++: glmark2's own source, fetched at its release and patched (ports/glmark2), built with its GLESv2 and EGL flavour.
Its options are glmark2's (`--help` lists them).
With none it runs its default benchmarks, each scene for ten seconds, printing each one's frames a second and frame time, and at the end the score, their mean.

It loads EGL and GLES as glmark2 does elsewhere, opening `libEGL.so` and `libGLESv2.so` with dlopen (dlfcn(2)) and asking for each function by name.
Those are our GLES library's, in bootfs's `lib/`; the program names them as libraries it needs, so the process that starts it loads them, with the Swift runtime they use, and dlopen finds them loaded.
Its display is EGL's default one, and its window a window of Radharc's of the size `--size` gives (800 by 600 unless it says otherwise), titled `glmark2`: the manifest says `use windows`.
`--off-screen` draws to a framebuffer of its own instead, waiting for each frame (`glFinish`); its window is then a headless one (egl(2)), which needs no compositor.

Its models, shaders and textures are `/lib/glmark2` (glmark2's `GLMARK_DATA_PATH`), bootfs's `lib/glmark2` mounted there by its manifest.
It carries libpng, libjpeg-turbo and zlib, compiled into it alone (ports/glmark2/README.md says which releases).

On the Orange Pi 6 Plus it is an app of the desktop image, started by the launcher (`echo start glmark2 >/svc/launcher/ctl`) once Radharc is up.
On the board, `esp-board-glmark2` (built on request) runs it off-screen at 800 by 600 with the board image's drivers and no desktop, until it ends, then reboots: the run the reference on AbyssBSD is compared with (docs/boards/orangepi-6-plus/gl.md), and the run that judges its budgets (below).
The launcher exits with its code (`launcher: glmark2-offscreen exited with <code>`).
In QEMU, `esp-glmark2` (built on request: `ninja -C build/arm64 esp-glmark2`) has userboot start it with no arguments; with no manifest there is no `/lib/glmark2`, so it says it can't open the models and textures directories, and with no GPU's EGL it stops at loading the EGL library.

# BUDGETS

Each scene of the default run is a budget, printed after the scene's own line as

```text
glmark2: budget name=gl.glmark2.<scene> value=<ns> unit=ns limit=<ns>
```

Its value is the scene's frame time; its limit is the time of a frame at 98% of the reference's frames a second for that scene, AbyssBSD's Panfrost on the Orange Pi 6 Plus at 800 by 600 off-screen (docs/boards/orangepi-6-plus/gl.md).
A budget line's limit is a ceiling, so a rate is printed as the time of one of its frames: a value at the limit or above it misses, and so a scene below 98% of the reference's rate misses.
The scenes, in the default run's order: `build.use-vbo-false`, `build.use-vbo-true`, `texture.nearest`, `texture.linear`, `texture.mipmap`, `shading.gouraud`, `shading.blinn-phong-inf`, `shading.phong`, `shading.cel`, `bump.high-poly`, `bump.normals`, `bump.height`, `effect2d.3x3`, `effect2d.5x3`, `pulsar`, `desktop.blur`, `desktop.shadow`, `buffer.map`, `buffer.subdata`, `buffer.interleave-map`, `ideas`, `jellyfish`, `terrain`, `shadow`, `refract`, `conditionals.f0-v0`, `conditionals.f5-v0`, `conditionals.f0-v5`, `function.low`, `function.medium`, `loop.no-fragment-loop`, `loop.constant` and `loop.uniform`.
A scene of the default run that is unsupported or fails to set up misses its budget: `glmark2: budget gl.glmark2.<scene>: the scene did not run`.
Once every scene of the default run has run, the score is a budget too, after glmark2's score line: `gl.glmark2.score`, one second over the score, against a frame at 98% of the reference's score (3064).
The last line is `glmark2: budgets met`, or `glmark2: <n> budget(s) over:` and their names; with any over, glmark2 exits with 1.
A run of other scenes (`-b`) judges those of the default run's that it ran, says how many of them ran, and has no score budget; scenes with other options have none.
The limits are the Orange Pi 6 Plus's, whatever GPU glmark2 runs on: `esp-board-glmark2`'s run is the one they judge, its verdict its last line.

